:: Michael Hang Out Park Playground Bully [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> head over to the pond as you listen to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> complain about classwork, homework, and just everything ‘work’ in general. He likes to rant a lot, but at least he does so in a humorous way. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I mean, when am I going to need anything past basic math? I’m not a nerd, I ain’t gonna go into some magic computer field. Just a waste of time, you know?”</span> You laugh at his description of computer science as the two of you walk to the edge of the pond. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Michael",
            State: {
                Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                Mouth: "Smirk",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> bends down and picks up a stone, telling you to <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Watch this”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">as he skips it across the pond impressively, bouncing 4 times.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Hah! Not bad, right? Whenever I go camping with my little cousin we like to skip rocks. It’s all about the wrist and shape of the rock…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> explains, finding a rock for you to toss and helping you move your wrist right. <span style="color:Pink">If you didn’t know any better, you’d think he was acting like a big brother.</span> <br>
<br>
But that doesn’t last, <span style="color:Yellow">as a sudden splash and a young gasp turn your attention a bit down the pond as you both see a young boy whose toy car had drove off-course and splashed down into the water. He looks at it worriedly, crawling to the edge of the rocks as he tries to reach it, but his arms are just too short.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>, losing all elements of tenderness you briefly saw, breaks out laughing. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Nice driving kid! Maybe try using your eyes next time, eh? Well, if you can get it out of the pond that is.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> <span style="color:Yellow">laughs harshly, the young boy blushing in embarrassment as he tries to reach the toy to no avail.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Go help the kid<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        Frowning at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>, you run over to help the kid out. You hear <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> call out <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Really? Fine, be a little hero. Just don’t blame me if you fall in.”</span> He chuckles as you kneel down next to the boy and try to help him reach the car. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> watches with amusement as he skips more rocks, occasionally shouting teasing comments. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">You nearly fall in but manage to just get ahold of the car and pull it out. The boy smiles widely as you do, sighing in relief and taking it happily.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Thank you!”</span> He says with a big smile before running off to dry off his toy. You sigh and smile, happy to do a good deed, as you walk back over to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>. <span style="color:Yellow">Once you get to him, he instantly wraps his arm around you and pulls you into a tight headlock!</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Michael",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“There’s my little hero! I should start calling you <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> Jr.!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He laughs, giving you a playful but painful noogie,</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“But hey, he would have fallen in. So maybe you can be the senior hero.”</span> He continues to tease and mess with you, though isn’t overly aggressive. <span style="color:Pink">Somehow, this feels even more like big brother energy than before.</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 15>>
        <<socialChange "Michael" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Michael Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 15>>
        <span style="color:green">+Michael Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Michael Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Join in on the laughter<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:Pink">You join in on the teasing, calling out your own mocking comment about how the boy will probably have to swim for his toy.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> laughs at this, patting you on the back. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ah, come on now <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$MichaelNickname</span>, you’re going to make him cry! Look, I can already see tears forming!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> points at the boy, <span style="color:Pink">only adding to his self-consciousness as he blushes and tries to turn away,</span> desperately reaching for his toy. <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Michael",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:Yellow">Then – splash – the boy loses his balance and stumbles into the shallow body of water, drenching himself in water.</span> <span style="color:Pink">Naturally, you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> both break out laughing at the boy’s misfortune.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Damn, who would have saw that coming!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> <span style="color:Pink">mocks as the little boy’s eyes well up in embarrassment and discomfort. Forgetting about his toy, he gets to his feet and runs off crying.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh, come on! Don’t be such a baby!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> calls out as he runs away, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Kids today are too soft. Come on, let’s go out of here before he gets his mommy to give us an earful.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> head off to another part of the park, continuing to joke about and mock the kid as you do. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> very much seems to get enjoyment out of the failures of others. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“He should have just walked in and grabbed it. He’d have gotten a little wet, but that’s the price you gotta pay when you fuck up.”</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 15>>
        <<socialChange "Michael" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Michael Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 15>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Michael Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<requiresTrait "Good" "Scold Michael">>
	<<replace"#choice">>
        <span style="color:LightCoral">Frowning, you wave your finger at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> and scold him for making fun of the kid. Crashing into the pond was an accident and all his teasing is doing is making the kid feel worse than he already does. Playful teasing is one thing, but this is just mean-spirited bullying, and you won’t stand for it, even if he is your friend. He should be ashamed of himself for picking on such a younger kid!</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Michael",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Woah, man. Chill out, I’m just messing.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> holds his hands up, blushing a bit as you scold him, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“No need to go all mom-mode on me.”</span> He tries to laugh it off, but you make your annoyance at his actions clear. He can’t just laugh and move on; he needs to make this right. You put your foot down and tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> to go over there and help the kid out as an apology for making fun of it. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Hey, I don’t gotta do nothing-!”</span> You wag your finger once more, repeating yourself and demanding he go up the kid. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“But I-”</span> <span style="color:Pink"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> seems completely stunned by your words, not expecting you to suddenly lecture him on being good. But it seems to do the job, as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> sighs before walking over to the boy grumbling to himself about you being a <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“goody two-shoes.”</span> The boy looks a little worried as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> comes over, but then smiles as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> manages to lean over and pull his car out of the water, handing it back to him while continuing to grumble. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Thank you!”</span> The little boy says happily, hugging <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>’s leg.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Michael",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                        Blush: 2,
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Wha- whatever!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> blushes, pulling the kid off of him. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Just watch where you’re going next time! Or else you may not get it back!”</span> The kid nods and runs off, happy to have his toy back as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> walks back over to you. <span style="color:Pink">You smile at him, proud that he did the right thing, but this just seems to annoy <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Stop looking at me like that, you freak! Come on, let’s go do something else before I start to bully you instead!”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:Pink">Despite his words, you are proud the boy seems to have learned from this experience.</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 15>>
        <<socialChange "Michael" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Michael Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 15>>
        <span style="color:green">+Michael Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Michael Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</requiresTrait>>
</div>